{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwfdUVygYoETBwJCAMpU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. It has already run once with status \"ok\", so its query works against the index.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** `kibana_sample_data_logs` has about 14,000 web requests, timestamped from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03 (so part of it is in the future). Each record has:\n- response code (`response`), bytes sent, client IP\n- host, URL, file extension\n- operating system, source and destination country, user agent and referrer\n\nThere are only three response codes: 200 (12,832 requests), 404 (801) and 503 (441).\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-b0d892cc Web logs overview\"** ([open it](http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-b0d892cc-web-logs-overview-0b65f85a8dc7)) has 7 panels:\n- Single-number panels for total requests, unique visitors (by client IP) and total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of each response code\n- Top 10 URLs, with request count and bytes\n- Top 10 source countries\n\nThe default time range is now−7d to now+60d so that the future-dated data shows up.\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-b0d892cc 5xx spike\"** (id `136047be-b88d-46b3-86a6-0f0261d1373b`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 requests with a response code starting with \"5\" (500–599) arrive within 5 minutes, based on the `timestamp` field.\n\nTwo things to know about the rule:\n- **It has no notification attached.** An alert is recorded in Kibana when it fires, but nobody gets an email or message. Adding one needs a connector (email, Slack, etc.).\n- **It will rarely fire on this sample data.** The data averages about 7 errors (503s) per day, so more than 10 in 5 minutes is unlikely unless there's a real spike."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":660,"cache_read_input_tokens":21642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":660},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"719525b4-b0f7-42a2-a445-6f88b1a628e4","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:54:10.644Z","request_id":"req_011CfwfdUDMurnEephgpnfzL"}
